              "tool_use_id": "toolu_01GDpBq5wVqpP9ETdrRk1ZC2",
              "type": "tool_result",
              "content": "1\t\\section{Discussion}\n2\t\\label{sec:discussion}\n3\t\n4\tSymbolic confirmation bias unifies two degradation channels: the \\emph{direct} channel limits voting diversity (Eff-$K < 2$), while the \\emph{indirect} channel causes MAX-SAT to degenerate to vote counting. The bias ratio gradient ($4.97\\times$ Mistral $> 3.93\\times$ Qwen $> 2.88\\times$ LLaMA) suggests weaker models suffer more severe confirmation bias, and the cross-architecture NLI experiment (\\S\\ref{sec:cross-arch}) corroborates that complementary signal must come from outside the model's distribution. Stronger models show higher SICA-SC convergence (Gemma-2-7B: 99.5\\% overlap, only 1/204 discordant), confirming confirmation bias intensifies with model capability---consistent with Qwen3 thinking mode degeneration ($\\kappa = 0.91$). For practitioners, $C_0$ combined with SC accuracy predicts when augmentation is unlikely to help. The oracle ceiling ($+14.22$\\,pp on FOLIO; \\S\\ref{sec:oracle}) shows that ${\\sim}$76\\% of the potential gain remains unrealized by self-extraction, motivating future work on trained extractors or hybrid verification methods. Whether 70B+ models shift the observed trade-off boundary is open."
            }
          ],
